{
  "_fixture_provenance": {
    "stage": "G6 - Eventbrite API feasibility investigation",
    "date": "2026-10-04",
    "sanitised": true,
    "contains_no_credentials": true,
    "shape_source": [
      "Live unauthenticated read-only probes against https://www.eventbriteapi.com on 2026-10-04 established the envelope: every /v3/* path returns 401 NO_AUTH without a token; /v3/events/search/ returns 404 NOT_FOUND (endpoint retired). Those envelopes are captured verbatim below.",
      "The official Eventbrite JavaScript SDK (github.com/eventbrite/eventbrite-sdk-javascript, master) establishes the documented resource model: GET /users/me/, GET /users/{user_id}/organizations/, page/page_size plus a `continuation` cursor, and an Organization object of {id, name, image_id, locale, vertical}.",
      "The collection envelope {pagination:{object_count,page_number,page_size,page_count,continuation,has_more_items}, events:[...]} and the event-object field set follow the documented Eventbrite v3 shapes."
    ],
    "fabrication_notice": "No live authenticated response was obtainable in this environment: no Eventbrite token exists in .env, Docker or the local WordPress option (see the G6 report). The event payloads below are therefore SHAPE-FIXTURES constructed to the documented v3 field names and semantics. They are NOT a capture of a real authenticated response and must not be cited as one."
  },

